            <ArticleTitle>Acute coronary events following cisplatin-based chemotherapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>583-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Six patients with no previous signs or symptoms suggestive of coronary artery disease developed acute coronary ischemia/infarction shortly after cis-diamine-dichloroplatinum II (cisplatin) -based chemotherapy. In two patients this was the sole chemotherapeutic agent used. One patient underwent coronary angiography which disclosed no pathology, but following which, while on a calcium channel blocking agent regimen, he had an uneventful course of chemotherapy with cisplatin. Documentation of cisplatin-related vascular events is important in view of the growing number of patients who undergo cisplatin-based chemotherapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
